# Line-ending policy.
#
# The repository history is already 100% LF (verified: `git ls-files --eol`
# reports zero `i/crlf` / `i/mixed` blobs). Git for Windows ships with a
# system-level `core.autocrlf=true`, which was re-writing ~444 tracked text
# files with CRLF in the working tree and showing them as spuriously
# "modified" with no real content change. Pinning the policy here makes it
# independent of each machine's Git config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit binary — never normalize, never diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.mp3  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.wav  binary
*.m4a  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.pdf  binary

